        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A mixture of GdCl3·6H2O (185.85 mg, 0.5 mmol), HL (127.16 mg, 1.0 mmol; HL = 2-pyridinethiol 1-oxide), 278.0 μL of triethylamine (2.0 mmol), and 8 mL of CH3OH was sealed in a Teflon-lined autoclave and heated at 130 °C for 24 h. After cooling to room temperature over 48 h, light-yellow block crystals of 1 were obtained, washed with methanol (5 × 4.0 mL), separated from white flocculent impurities under an optical microscope, and dried in air at room temperature to give a desolvated/hydrated species analyzed as 1.",
